h4. Article 20.2 – ZBE access (Zona de Baixas Emisións)

*Summary:* Within the designated ZBE CENTRO (Old Town, Av. da Marina, Parrote, and certain Pescadería streets), access/circulation is restricted to:

* *Public transport*;
* *Taxis* but *only* along Av. da Marina–Avda. Montoto–Porta Real–Cidade Vella;
* *Authorized vehicles*;
* *Loading/unloading vehicles* within specific morning time windows, extended for vehicles with certain environmental labels;
* *Public-service vehicles* (with an *8-meter length limit* inside Cidade Vella);
* *Vehicles to reserved/authorized spaces*.

----

h4. Article 70.6 – Taxis in pedestrian areas

*Summary:* Taxis are *authorized to drive in pedestrian streets* *only* to serve *holders of mobility-reduced accreditation*. Each trip that *starts or ends* in a pedestrian zone must be *previously communicated to the Local Police* via the medium established in each case.

----

h4. Article 73 – Legal regime for VTC (vehicles with driver)

*Summary:* Urban passenger transport by *VTC* is governed by *state and regional law* (LOTT/RLOTT; Galicia’s Law 4/2013 and Decree 103/2018). Under *Law 4/2013, art. 46*, municipalities must regulate via *specific ordinances* the *grant/conditions/limits* for VTC *urban* services; *without such a specific ordinance*, *authorizations enabling urban VTC services cannot be granted*, nor may the service be provided. Any authorizations/limits for urban VTC require that *specific ordinance*.

